<v Mike>I mean, I don't know any console today giving you three games.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:05.980
<v Sean>Even two controllers. Right.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.240
<v Mike>Three games, two controllers, and two accessories.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:17.880
<v Joe>Damn. Yeah, for like, I mean, by your translation there, it's for still less than like a base PS5, right?

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.840
<v Sean>Or a Switch 2.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:25.520
<v Mike>Yeah. But is this the best of the pack-ins just because it adds another game?

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.540
<v Mike>Like, does it make the most sense?

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:34.900
<v Mike>Is there a different game that they could pack in, with or without all the accessories, for a better value?

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.980
<v Mike>Like, could we have pushed for just a-

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:37.860
<v Sean>Almost any game.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:50.620
<v Joe>Yeah, right. I guess what I meant is-

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.900
<v Mike>I mean, I think the elf still had the ethos of like, this is going to be cool.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.100
<v Joe>I guess if you're trying to get the power pad worked in, I see why they went with this.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:07.640
<v Sean>I know that we kind of have some time dilation going on with like how we actually experience every release on this like console.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:15.520
<v Sean>But like, you know the Kinect, like I feel like this is at the time when everyone already knew that the Kinect was a joke.

